			rgCommunityRecommendations: [{"appid":4833450,"reviews":[{"recommendationid":"234010703","appid":4833450,"accountid":241801025,"playtime_at_review":60,"review_text":"I wasn't quite sure what to expect or even if I would like this game, bought it without thinking (and a lil drunk) BUT, this is so much more than I thought it is The graphics are phantastic, very psychedelic at times, it...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198202066753\/recommended\/4833450\/","votes_up":10},{"recommendationid":"233996285","appid":4833450,"accountid":85457874,"playtime_at_review":381,"review_text":"An incredible experience. A true piece of freak literature made by gross perverts, and I cannot recommend it enough. Emotionally moving and wonderful, I think it will stay with me for a long time.","review_text_truncated":false,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198045723602\/recommended\/4833450\/","votes_up":5},{"recommendationid":"234030582","appid":4833450,"accountid":130603638,"playtime_at_review":150,"review_text":"Disco Elysium for fans of Doki Doki Literature Club with a Madoka Magica witchy aesthetic. Great ost, funny too. If you're a fan of visual novel style gameplay and also a sick little freak you need to play this game asap.","review_text_truncated":false,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198090869366\/recommended\/4833450\/","votes_up":6}]},{"appid":3516590,"reviews":[{"recommendationid":"233997630","appid":3516590,"accountid":244805275,"playtime_at_review":424,"review_text":"The game has great bones. It's early access, and I look forward to what it will become. For now, buy it knowing that it is very early days. It's also a beautiful game.","review_text_truncated":false,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198205071003\/recommended\/3516590\/","votes_up":5}]},{"appid":2161700,"reviews":[{"recommendationid":"234001994","appid":2161700,"accountid":1741372733,"playtime_at_review":5363,"review_text":"Put nearly 90 hrs into P3R n cleared the whole thing. People online got all kinds of hot takes on the story, but I\u2019m firmly team this game goes hard. If I had to nail the whole game\u2019s vibe in one word - Farewell. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561199701638461\/recommended\/2161700\/","votes_up":36}]},{"appid":3849000,"reviews":[{"recommendationid":"234030646","appid":3849000,"accountid":54085144,"playtime_at_review":293,"review_text":"LIZARD MEN I haven't found the Epstien Island dungeon yet I am level 1 and I don't care I WILL beat my head against the brick wall until I beat it. It has drugs and fantasy racism, welcome back, Dagoth Ur. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198014350872\/recommended\/3849000\/","votes_up":4}]},{"appid":2492670,"reviews":[{"recommendationid":"233999079","appid":2492670,"accountid":1521100,"playtime_at_review":1546,"review_text":"Just buy the game. It's so good that I finished it in one sitting without ever feeling bored or tired. The gameplay feels amazing, and the audio design is really well done, especially with its positioning and overall...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561197961786828\/recommended\/2492670\/","votes_up":192},{"recommendationid":"234052058","appid":2492670,"accountid":115477042,"playtime_at_review":279,"review_text":"\"Solid\" remaster (huh?). I absolutely love this game's cast, and I genuinely believe MGS4 occupies a unique place within the series. Sure, the original MGS1 is probably untouchable, unreplicable, and unbeatable. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198075742770\/recommended\/2492670\/","votes_up":11},{"recommendationid":"234036878","appid":2492670,"accountid":393603055,"playtime_at_review":984,"review_text":"\u201cBoss... you only need one Snake... no... the world would be better off without Snakes...\u201d The last Metal Gear Solid game and honestly the perfect ending to the series. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198353868783\/recommended\/2492670\/","votes_up":5},{"recommendationid":"234016121","appid":2492670,"accountid":396347735,"playtime_at_review":915,"review_text":"There is no better game to conclude a saga than Metal Gear Solid 4. Playing every MGS game beforehand makes this one of the most rewarding video game experiences there is. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198356613463\/recommended\/2492670\/","votes_up":6},{"recommendationid":"234006309","appid":2492670,"accountid":119395428,"playtime_at_review":295,"review_text":"My favorite game to play on ps3. This game is the peak of cooperation between Kojima and Konami, before everything went sour with phantom pain. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198079661156\/recommended\/2492670\/","votes_up":3},{"recommendationid":"234014815","appid":2492670,"accountid":67226247,"playtime_at_review":963,"review_text":"They told me to switch to disc 2 but then they remembered this is on Steam 10\/10. This and MGS3 are the best games in the series and despite being made in 2008 its 100% relateable for 2026 both story wise and gamewise. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198027491975\/recommended\/2492670\/","votes_up":4}]},{"appid":3241660,"reviews":[{"recommendationid":"233991801","appid":3241660,"accountid":1862878774,"playtime_at_review":518,"review_text":"One of the best friend-slop games so far for me. I've made so many great memories with my friends in this game; and I would say it's worth the $ because we can always get back to it any time we want to bond together. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561199823144502\/recommended\/3241660\/","votes_up":4}]},{"appid":4075620,"reviews":[{"recommendationid":"233992947","appid":4075620,"accountid":109984641,"playtime_at_review":254,"review_text":"Excellent minimalist roguelike that packs a punch of replayability and content. Every run feels like you're building something unique and special. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198070250369\/recommended\/4075620\/","votes_up":8}]},{"appid":2749950,"reviews":[{"recommendationid":"234006153","appid":2749950,"accountid":836049499,"playtime_at_review":13988,"review_text":"The people leaving this negative reviews are crazy. The update made the game 100x times better. \"AI SLOP!1!111!!\" You simply go into the workshop or the embd.gg site and download a real world database that has all real life...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198796315227\/recommended\/2749950\/","votes_up":4}]},{"appid":2075800,"reviews":[{"recommendationid":"234038758","appid":2075800,"accountid":399894032,"playtime_at_review":1449,"review_text":"Great Game. Its a lot more than just XCOM meets Star Wars. If you like Star Wars\/tactical turn-based RPGs I think you will have fun with this game. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198360159760\/recommended\/2075800\/","votes_up":16}]},{"appid":534380,"reviews":[{"recommendationid":"234062634","appid":534380,"accountid":994768325,"playtime_at_review":2904,"review_text":"Dying Light 2 is such a great game. I understand why some people don't like it as much as the first game, but it was still such a great experience. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198955034053\/recommended\/534380\/","votes_up":6}]},{"appid":2492660,"reviews":[{"recommendationid":"234012766","appid":2492660,"accountid":296017277,"playtime_at_review":235,"review_text":"Metal Gear Solid: Peace Walker is a really special game, and having pretty much all of the MGS games in the volume collection is a real treat. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198256283005\/recommended\/2492660\/","votes_up":6},{"recommendationid":"234016739","appid":2492660,"accountid":1558180821,"playtime_at_review":1883,"review_text":"This game was life-changing. Waited for it for about 6 months,it was 100% worth the wait. The lore and gameplay are genuinely insane for a PSP. Defenetly my favourite MGS game.","review_text_truncated":false,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561199518446549\/recommended\/2492660\/","votes_up":4},{"recommendationid":"234038342","appid":2492660,"accountid":89766889,"playtime_at_review":1981,"review_text":"A 1:1 port of the old HD collection version of Peace Walker, without any of the cameos or easter eggs removed. With co-op and vs as well even brought back. For this reason alone its perfect. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198050032617\/recommended\/2492660\/","votes_up":4}]},{"appid":2713000,"reviews":[{"recommendationid":"233991962","appid":2713000,"accountid":159138456,"playtime_at_review":1205,"review_text":"I love this game so much! As a Plague Tale fan who adores the first two games, it is really nice to see Asobo shaking things up with different gameplay. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198119404184\/recommended\/2713000\/","votes_up":26},{"recommendationid":"234040604","appid":2713000,"accountid":1145016569,"playtime_at_review":1246,"review_text":"Puzzles, aggressive combat, chases, and stealth from a monster... this game has everything I enjoy, and I honestly never got bored the entire time I was playing it. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561199105282297\/recommended\/2713000\/","votes_up":7},{"recommendationid":"234069922","appid":2713000,"accountid":1206660358,"playtime_at_review":1035,"review_text":"A Masterpiece I Did Not Know I Needed After finishing both [A Plague Tale: Innocence and Requiem].... I was left with that familiar... hollow feeling.... the desperate need for more. ...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561199166926086\/recommended\/2713000\/","votes_up":4},{"recommendationid":"234033256","appid":2713000,"accountid":458869915,"playtime_at_review":1132,"review_text":"This game is soooooooooo good, asobo knows how to make story games, game performance is amazing, graphic fidelity too.","review_text_truncated":false,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561198419135643\/recommended\/2713000\/","votes_up":3},{"recommendationid":"234039325","appid":2713000,"accountid":1202899276,"playtime_at_review":1075,"review_text":"Finished Resonance in around ~18 hours, I think it works surprisingly well as both a Plague Tale game and as a standalone experience. You don't really need to have played Innocence or Requiem beforehand to enjoy it (in my...","review_text_truncated":true,"review_link":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/profiles\/76561199163165004\/recommended\/2713000\/","votes_up":2}]}],
